cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A Price-Time Priority Order Book Simulator, a Controlled Liquidity Stress Experiment, and the Cost of Ignoring the Queue"
abstract: >-
  A limit order book matching engine with exchange-style price-time
  priority, verified by invariant checks, a differential test against a
  brute-force matcher and a 15-bug reintroduction harness. On calibrated
  zero-intelligence order flow (synthetic only), a pre-specified sell burst
  widens the spread by a median 1.18 ticks with recovery in under a minute,
  and passive probe orders that a naive instant-fill assumption books at
  1.40 ticks of spread earned actually pay 0.26 ticks once queue position
  is modelled.
